{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_57","type":"agent_message","text":"The mitigation is submitted and accepted (`stage: mitigation`).\n\n**Root cause:** The `otelu` role's password in PostgreSQL didn't match the one every consumer uses (`otelp_7k9m2q4x`, per `init.sql`, the `product-catalog-db-conn` secret, and the product-reviews and accounting deployments). Product-catalog's connections were rejected with `password authentication failed`, which broke product lookups. Recommendation and the frontend then returned `Product Not Found` / errors.\n\n**Changes made:**\n- `ALTER USER otelu WITH PASSWORD 'otelp_7k9m2q4x'` in the `postgresql` pod. I verified SCRAM over TCP accepts the correct password and rejects a wrong one.\n- Restarted `deploy/product-catalog` so it re-established connections with the correct credential.\n- Temporarily enabled `log_connections` to find the failing client, then reset it to default.\n\n**Verification:** Postgres auth failures and recommendation errors dropped to zero, frontend errors were zero over a 30-second window, and all app pods are Running.\n\n**Not fixed (outside the mitigation):**\n- The `accounting` pod (nightly image) crash-loops with `Cannot load library libgssapi_krb5.so.2`. It is not user-facing, but it will need an image or library fix.\n- The database password is hardcoded in plaintext in deployment specs and `init.sql`, and the password was out of sync with the one used by the consumers. Moving it into a single Secret would prevent a repeat."}}
